# y8 trim fragment (2026-10-15, final): config options for hardware/features the owner does not use.
# 538 "is not set" + 10 "=m" lines. Every symbol below is =y or =m in inventory/config-running and was
# checked against inventory/bound-drivers, lsmod, modules.builtin, class-members, input-devices, mounts,
# packages, apps and the board DT (tb323fu-linux/kernel/dts). Unused drivers that are not bound cost
# RAM/boot time when built in (=y) and only disk/build time when =m; they do NOT cost runtime power.
#
# Apply AFTER config-t49.release (kbuild-y8.sh): for each line run
#   scripts/config --file .config --disable X   (for "# CONFIG_X is not set")
#   scripts/config --file .config --module  X   (for "CONFIG_X=m")
# then `make olddefconfig`, then check the MUST-KEEP list (y8-must-keep.txt) mechanically: every symbol
# there must still be =y / =m. kbuild-y8.sh must DROP the "CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDERFS=y must survive" check
# (section K) and keep the ntsync / zram zstd / exfat / MGLRU / BTF checks.
#
# Provenance: many of these were switched ON deliberately upstream - the OnePlus 15 defconfig (patch 0011:
# IR_SPI, RC_CORE, TYPEC_TCPM/QCOM_PMIC, QRTR_TUN, binder, PM_WAKELOCKS, BLK_DEV_RAM, F2FS=y) and the t49
# baldur-extra.fragment test devices (VKMS/VGEM, IIO dummy, SND_DUMMY, DUMMY_HCD, RAW_GADGET, GPIO_SIM,
# VIVID/VIMC, F_UVC/F_MIDI/F_PRINTER, USB_PRINTER). This file reverses those on purpose for this tablet;
# when the base config is upgraded (t5x), re-apply it rather than treating the lines as omissions.
# Risk legend in the comments: [low] / [medium]. Nothing here touches a stability workaround
# (QCOM_WDT, DPM_WATCHDOG, lockup/hung-task panics, allow_cluster_off, MMU-500 CPRE errata stay).

# ---- A. Virtualisation [low]: Linux runs at EL1 under the firmware hypervisor (dmesg "All CPU(s) started at EL1"),
#      KVM is not even configured, qemu is installed but never used (README: qemu-kvm.service is a stray enablement).
#      All built in today: xen frontends, virtio pci/mmio/blk/net/console/balloon/rng, vfio-pci, pv steal clock.
# CONFIG_XEN is not set
# CONFIG_XEN_DOM0 is not set
# CONFIG_PARAVIRT is not set
# CONFIG_VFIO is not set
# CONFIG_VHOST_MENU is not set
# CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI is not set
# CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO is not set
# CONFIG_VIRTIO_BALLOON is not set
